         """Rows to re-draw and their parents. The guard is on ``flagged`` (all rows flagged this evaluation): nothing is done while more than Q of the
         table is flagged (most of the table still in transit has no support to clone from; the same level as the test). The rows re-drawn are
         ``act`` (default: ``flagged``; the trainer passes the rows flagged in two consecutive evaluations) minus the rows the ordinary moves just
-        re-drew. Each becomes a clone of an unflagged row drawn among the k^2 nearest unflagged rows in the table's own latent space, with probability
-        proportional to ``weight`` (the row's own isolation p-value: the mass without support goes back into the nearest supported neighbourhood and
-        into its bulk, not its rim: rim rows have small p and their clones are flagged again). The rank cap keeps the rule local in any latent
-        dimension."""
+        re-drew. Each becomes a clone of an unflagged row drawn among the (at most k^2 nearest) unflagged rows in the table's own latent space that are at
+        most twice as far as its nearest unflagged row, with probability proportional to ``weight`` (the row's own isolation p-value: the mass without
+        support goes back into the nearest supported neighbourhood, into its bulk and not its rim: rim rows have small p and their clones are flagged
+        again). The distance limit keeps the mass in the nearest neighbourhood also when that neighbourhood has fewer than k^2 rows (the first rows
+        that arrive at a mode after a shift: a rank cap alone would then draw parents from other modes and shuffle mass, as uniform parents do); the rank
+        cap keeps the rule local in any latent dimension."""
